  ok\ ---- section-marker: makes this file independently runnable ----
  ok\ M26 snapshots the dictionary/HERE state right before this
  ok\ file's own definitions begin. Invoking M26 at the end (below)
  ok\ erases everything this file defined - including M26 itself -
  ok\ restoring the system to the state it was in just after
  ok\ ttester.fs + 00_test_prelude.fs were loaded. This lets the
  ok\ automation load/run/reset one section file at a time, in any
  ok\ order, without cross-file dictionary pollution.
  okMARKER M26
  ok\ Reset the pass/fail counters, record the stack depth.
  okTEST-BEGIN
  ok\ F.9.6.2.0670  ABORT
  ok\ See F.9.6.2.0680 ABORT".
  ok\ F.9.6.2.0680  ABORT" - exc_undef (-13) and the OF branch values need
  ok\ DECIMAL; saved/restored locally rather than a bare DECIMAL, for
  ok\ the same reason as the other files this round (this one happens
  ok\ to be last in load order, so nothing downstream is affected
  ok\ today, but there's no guarantee it stays last).
  ok\ BUG FIX (round 1): was "BASE @ >R DECIMAL ... R> BASE !" - unsafe
  ok\ spanning separate top-level lines (see 08_defining_words.tests.fs's
  ok\ matching comment for the full >R/R> mechanism).
  ok\ BUG FIX (round 2): plain "BASE @ DECIMAL ... BASE !" is also
  ok\ fragile here - this file tests ABORT/ABORT"/CATCH directly, a
  ok\ plausible source of an uncaught error that would wipe a parked
  ok\ stack value via QLOOP's top-level recovery. Unconditional restore
  ok\ instead - see 08_defining_words.tests.fs for the full reasoning.
  okDECIMAL
  ok-1 CONSTANT exc_abort
  ok-2 CONSTANT exc_abort"
  ok-13 CONSTANT exc_undef
  ok: t6 ABORT ;
  ok: t10 77 SWAP ABORT" This should not be displayed" ;
  ok: c6 CATCH
CASE exc_abort OF 11 ENDOF
exc_abort" OF 12 ENDOF
exc_undef OF 13 ENDOF
ENDCASE
